#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Is any Actor README big enough that Apify's Store page silently truncates it?
(added cycle 3809, following up on NEW c3808a)

c3808 found this by accident while verifying an unrelated push: the build record's
`readme` field for remote-jobs-scraper (131,715 local bytes) came back at EXACTLY
99,999 chars, and probing the rendered Store page (grep for backticked rival handles
at known local byte offsets) showed the render truncates with the stored field --
offset 99,900 was on the page, 100,677 was not, nor was anything out to 107,944.
Measured blast radius at c3808: SIX Actors over the cap (sam-gov-opportunities-scraper
134,566B losing ~34.6KB; remote-jobs-scraper 131,715B; ats-jobs-scraper 110,371B;
uk-find-a-tender-scraper 109,129B; hacker-news-scraper 109,038B;
trademark-search-scraper 107,064B), ~101KB of product copy invisible to buyers in
total, and nothing in the fleet watched README length against this cap --
check-doc-size watches tasks/queue.md and state/STATUS.md only.

The cap is measured, not Apify's documented number (if they publish one, it was not
found at c3808) -- RED_BYTES is the exact boundary observed live. WARN_BYTES gives a
cycle of runway before an Actor crosses it, the same two-tier shape check-doc-size
uses (WARN_BYTES/TRIM_BYTES there).

Read-only, no network, no cost: this only measures local actors/*/README.md byte
counts. It does NOT re-probe the rendered Store page (see NEW c3808a's method for
that one-off verification step, needed only once per fix, not every cadence run).
Exit 1 if any README is at/over RED_BYTES or at/over WARN_BYTES.
"""
import glob
import os
import sys

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))

RED_BYTES = 99_999   # measured live boundary, c3808: build record `readme` field truncates here
WARN_BYTES = 95_000  # ~1 cycle of runway at typical per-Actor README growth

flagged = warned = checked = 0
for path in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(ROOT, "actors/*/README.md"))):
    rel = os.path.relpath(path, ROOT)
    size = os.path.getsize(path)
    checked += 1
    if size >= RED_BYTES:
        flagged += 1
        print(f"RED  {rel}: {size:,}B -- at/over the {RED_BYTES:,}B truncation cap, Store page is losing {size - RED_BYTES:,}+ bytes of the tail")
    elif size >= WARN_BYTES:
        warned += 1
        print(f"WARN {rel}: {size:,}B -- within {RED_BYTES - size:,}B of the truncation cap")

print(f"check-readme-cap: {checked} README(s) checked, {flagged} over cap, {warned} within warn band")
sys.exit(1 if flagged else 0)
